+---
+id: task-002-implement-json-patch-applypatch-rfc-6902
+type: task
+title: "Implement JSON Patch applyPatch (RFC 6902)"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Request
+
+Implement JSON Patch (RFC 6902). Export `applyPatch(document, patch)` from `src/index.ts`; it applies an
+array of operations (add, remove, replace, move, copy, test) and returns the result as a new value.
+
+# Acceptance
+
+- The input document and the patch are never mutated, and the result shares no structure with them.
+- Throws when the patch is not an array, an operation is not an object, `op` is unknown, `path`/`from`
+  is missing or not a valid JSON Pointer, or `value` is missing where required.
+- add: inserts into arrays (index <= length, `-` appends) or sets/replaces an object member; `""` replaces
+  the document. remove/replace: the target must exist. move: `from` must exist and may not be a proper
+  prefix of `path`. copy: `from` must exist. test: deep equality (object member order ignored); a
+  mismatch throws.
+- A failing operation aborts the whole patch (the error is thrown, nothing is returned).
+- Members named `__proto__` are handled as ordinary members and never pollute prototypes.
